ironment","last_updated":"2026-09-27T08:07:27.782135","license":"","needs_review":false,"oa_status":"closed","oa_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.atmosenv.2025.121686","openalex_topics":["T10075","T10190","T12095"],"plastic_related":false,"plastic_tier":"","primary_topic":"T10075","pub_date":"2025-11-20","study_type":"article","title":"Contributions of tailpipe and non-tailpipe emissions to the oxidative potential of source-resolved PM10 from major LDV- and HDV-dominated freeways in Los Angeles","type":"article","work_id":"W4416418629","year":2025},{"abstract":"","author_count":13,"author_ids":["A5001328363","A5028077050","A5029277426","A5036057349","A5048754844","A5076250081","A5083525391","A5084487425","A5100639064","A5117726111","A5120431484","A5138388453","A5140529446"],"author_institution_ids":["I1174212"],"authors":[{"id":"A5120431484","name":"Sahar Fazelvalipour"},{"id":"A5036057349","name":"Y U E J I He"},{"id":"A5029277426","name":"Mohammad Mahdi Badami"},{"id":"A5117726111","name":"Diego Ramos Aguilera"},{"id":"A5138388453","name":"Venezia Ramirez"},{"id":"A5083525391","name":"Yashar Aghaei"},{"id":"A5001328363","name":"Vahid Jalali Farahani"},{"id":"A5140529446","name":"Yunhan Huang"},{"id":"A5084487425","name":"Mo Chen"},{"id":"A5028077050","name":"Sara D. Forestieri"},{"id":"A5076250081","name":"David C. Quiros"},{"id":"A5048754844","name":"Constantinos Sioutas"},{"id":"A5100639064","name":"Jiachen Zhang"}],"ca_any_author":true,"ca_led":true,"cited_by_count":0,"doi":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.envpol.2026.129520","domain_tags":["fate_transport_and_sorption"],"facet_tags":[],"institution_ids":["I1174212","I1316958739"],"is_oa":true,"journal":"Environmental Pollution","last_updated":"2026-11-27T09:11:17.138145","license":"","needs_review":false,"oa_status":"green","oa_url":"https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.7114236","openalex_topics":["T10768","T12095","T12126"],"plastic_related":false,"plastic_tier":"","primary_topic":"T12095","pub_date":"2026-11-12","study_type":"article","title":"Forgone Community Emission Benefits in Southern California Without Zero-Emission Truck Regulations","type":"article","work_id":"W7168186223","year":2026},{"abstract":"Airborne microplastics (MPs) are increasingly recognized as atmospheric pollutants with potential implications for human exposure; however, their occurrence, temporal variability, and associations with urban particulate matter remain poorly understood. This study investigated suspected MPs identified by optical microscopy associated with PM10 from central Los Angeles across two seasonal campaigns by integrating MP abundance, morphology, size distribution, PM10 chemical composition, and meteorological observations. Suspected MPs were detected in all samples, with concentrations ranging from 0.8\u20131.4 MP/m3 during the cool-season campaign and 0.7\u20131.1 MP/m3 during the warm-season campaign. Fibers remained the dominant morphology, while particles <100 \u00b5m, particularly the 5\u201350 \u00b5m and 50\u2013100 \u00b5m fractions, consistently dominated the airborne MP population. Total MP concentrations correlated positively with 15 of the 17 measured PM10 species, most strongly with Cr, Fe, Cu, Mn, and Mg (\u03c1 = 0.93\u20130.98). The associations with Cr, Cu, Ba, and Fe remained significant after controlling for PM10 mass, pointing to elements commonly linked to non-tailpipe traffic emissions and road dust. In contrast, short-term meteorological variability showed no consistent relationship with MP concentrations. These findings indicate that airborne suspected MPs are a persistent component of the urban PM10 mixture rather than isolated contaminants, and provide new insight into their behavior in densely populated urban environments.","author_count":8,"author_ids":["A5002529431","A5025419758","A5029277426","A5048754844","A5083525391","A5120431484","A5158027413","A5158057927"],"author_institution_ids":[],"authors":[{"id":"A5120431484","name":"Sahar Fazelvalipour"},{"id":"A5083525391","name":"Yashar Aghaei"},{"id":"A5029277426","name":"Mohammad Mahdi Badami"},{"id":"A5002529431","name":"Kanchana Chandrakanthan"},{"id":"A5025419758","name":"Pierre Herck\u00e8s"},{"id":"A5158057927","name":"Matthew P. Fraser"},{"id":"A5158027413","name":"Jiachen Zhang"},{"id":"A5048754844","name":"Constantinos Sioutas"}],"ca_any_author":true,"ca_led":true,"cited_by_count":0,"doi":"https://doi.org/10.3390/atmos17121172","domain_tags":["air","occurrence_and_monitoring"],"facet_tags":["matrix:air"],"institution_ids":[],"is_oa":true,"journal":"Atmosphere","last_updated":"2026-11-27T09:11:17.138145","license":"cc-by","needs_review":false,"oa_status":"gold","oa_url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/atmos17121172","openalex_topics":["T10075","T10419","T10753"],"plastic_related":true,"plastic_tier":"core","primary_topic":"T10753","pub_date":"2026-11-26","study_type":"article","title":"Size-Resolved Characteristics and Source Influences of Suspected Airborne Microplastics in Central Los Angeles: A Case Study","type":"article","work_id":"W7221132240","year":2026}]}
